#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:1
msgid "llvm-strip - object stripping tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:6
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:8
msgid "{program}`llvm-strip` \\[*options*\\] *inputs...*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:10
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:12
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-strip` is a tool to strip sections and symbols from object "
"files. If no other stripping or remove options are specified, {option}`--"
"strip-all` will be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:16
msgid ""
"By default, the input files are modified in-place. If \"-\" is specified for "
"the input file, the input is read from the program's standard input stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:19
msgid ""
"If the input is an archive, any requested operations will be applied to each "
"archive member individually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:22
msgid ""
"The tool is still in active development, but in most scenarios it works as a "
"drop-in replacement for GNU's {program}`strip`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:25
msgid "GENERIC AND CROSS-PLATFORM OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:27
msgid ""
"The following options are either agnostic of the file format, or apply to "
"multiple file formats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:31
msgid ""
"Use real values for UIDs, GIDs and timestamps when updating archive member "
"headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:36
msgid ""
"Remove most local symbols not referenced by relocations from the output. "
"Different file formats may limit this to a subset of the local symbols. For "
"example, file and section symbols in ELF objects will not be discarded. "
"Additionally, remove all debug sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:43
msgid ""
"Enable deterministic mode when stripping archives, i.e. use 0 for archive "
"member header UIDs, GIDs and timestamp fields. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:48
msgid "Print a summary of command line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:52
msgid "Disable {option}`--strip-all`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:56
msgid ""
"Write output to \\<file>. Multiple input files cannot be used in combination "
"with -o."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:61
msgid ""
"Produce a debug file as the output that only preserves contents of sections "
"useful for debugging purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:64
msgid ""
"For ELF objects, this removes the contents of `SHF_ALLOC` sections that are "
"not `SHT_NOTE` by making them `SHT_NOBITS` and shrinking the program headers "
"where possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:70
msgid ""
"If specified, symbol and section names specified by other switches are "
"treated as extended POSIX regular expression patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:75
msgid ""
"Remove the specified section from the output. Can be specified multiple "
"times to remove multiple sections simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:80
msgid ""
"Remove all symbols, debug sections and relocations from the output. This "
"option is equivalent to GNU {program}`strip`'s `--strip-all` switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:85
msgid ""
"For ELF objects, remove from the output all symbols and non-alloc sections "
"not within segments, except for .gnu.warning, .ARM.attribute sections and "
"the section name table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:89
msgid ""
"For COFF and Mach-O objects, remove all symbols, debug sections, and "
"relocations from the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:92
msgid ""
"For WebAssembly objects, remove all custom sections except for those named "
"metadata.code.\\*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:97
msgid "Remove all debug sections from the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:101
msgid ""
"Remove all symbols named `<symbol>` from the output. Can be specified "
"multiple times to remove multiple symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:106
msgid ""
"Remove from the output all local or undefined symbols that are not required "
"by relocations. Also remove all debug sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:111
msgid "Print the paths of files that are copied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:115
msgid "Display the version of the {program}`llvm-strip` executable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:119
msgid ""
"Allow wildcard syntax for symbol-related flags. On by default for section-"
"related flags. Incompatible with --regex."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:122
msgid "Wildcard syntax allows the following special symbols:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "Character"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "Equivalent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "`*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "Any number of characters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "`.*`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "`?`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "Any single character"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "`.`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "`\\`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "Escape the next character"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "`[a-z]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "Character class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "`[!a-z]`, `[^a-z]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "Negated character class"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:118
msgid "`[^a-z]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:132
msgid ""
"Additionally, starting a wildcard with '!' will prevent a match, even if "
"another flag matches. For example `-w -N '*' -N '!x'` will strip all symbols "
"except for `x`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:136
msgid ""
"The order of wildcards does not matter. For example, `-w -N '*' -N '!x'` is "
"the same as `-w -N '!x' -N '*'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:141
msgid "Read command-line options and commands from response file `<FILE>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:144
msgid "ELF-SPECIFIC OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:146
msgid ""
"The following options are implemented only for ELF objects. If used with "
"other objects, {program}`llvm-strip` will either emit an error or silently "
"ignore them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:151
msgid ""
"Allow {program}`llvm-strip` to remove sections even if it would leave "
"invalid section references. Any invalid sh_link fields will be set to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:156
msgid ""
"Remove local symbols starting with \".L\" not referenced by relocations from "
"the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:160
msgid ""
"Keep symbols of type `STT_FILE`, even if they would otherwise be stripped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:164
msgid ""
"When removing sections from the output, do not remove sections named "
"`<section>`. Can be specified multiple times to keep multiple sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:169
msgid ""
"When removing symbols from the output, do not remove symbols named "
"`<symbol>`. Can be specified multiple times to keep multiple symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:174
msgid "Preserve access and modification timestamps in the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:178
msgid ""
"Remove from the output all section headers and all section data not within "
"segments. Note that many tools will not be able to use an object without "
"section headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:183
msgid "MACH-O-SPECIFIC OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:185
msgid ""
"The following options are implemented only for Mach-O objects. If used with "
"other objects, {program}`llvm-strip` will either emit an error or silently "
"ignore them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:190
msgid "Remove Swift symbols."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:193
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:195
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-strip` exits with a non-zero exit code if there is an error. "
"Otherwise, it exits with code 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:198
msgid "BUGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-strip.md:200
msgid ""
"To report bugs, please visit \\<<https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/labels/"
"tools:llvm-objcopy%2Fstrip>>."
msgstr ""

